# Android Security Rules (OWASP MASVS)

- Sensitive tokens and credentials MUST be stored in `EncryptedSharedPreferences` or KeyStore. Never store secrets in raw `SharedPreferences`.
- Non-launcher components in `AndroidManifest.xml` must set `android:exported="false"`.
- Never allow cleartext HTTP (`android:usesCleartextTraffic="true"`).
- Cryptographically bind biometric auth via `BiometricPrompt.CryptoObject`.
- Never log PII in `Log.d` or `println`; use Timber with release stripping.
